      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 102: 🟡 Synced trust requests drop the sender-embedded invite timestamp by passing `invited` as `{}`. A second device that learns the request through account sync will order it by local receive time, while later DHT-delivered requests are ordered by sender `invitedMs`; with clock skew this can cause a legitimate re-invite to look older and be ignored. Persist/sync the invite timestamp with the trust request and pass it through here.",
